From 1900d01450cdbdf72e8fe6ca24f155d6226e5701 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Micheal Waltz <micheal@ecliptik.com>
Date: Thu, 5 Nov 2026 15:36:40 -0800
Subject: [PATCH] DOS-PORT: patch 0355 -- MIDI-only audio (model C) when the
 Sound Blaster cannot open

Without a Sound Blaster (no BLASTER variable, no DSP, or the stream would not open)
sys_audio_init() returned false, engine_init_audio() set AudioEnabled=false, and ALL
audio was off -- so an AdLib-only (OPL at 388h) or MPU-401-only machine played no music,
although opl3_sink and waveblaster_sink drive their ports directly and need no SB. Found
on the 486 (dosags R4 ADLC16, PicoGUS in AdLib mode: "No BLASTER environment variable"
-> "Audio is disabled").

Model C, reached only from those two SB-path failure returns and only for a hint naming
a MIDI backend that needs no SB (unset/auto/opl3, wb): the audio core and the MIDI
backend keep running; the mixer opens with NO PCM device (pcm=none@11025m16) and drains
active voices against uclock() at the device rate in 512-sample chunks, discarding them,
so a clip still ends after its real duration (a pump gap is credited at most 5 chunks,
~232 ms, about the SB path's queued depth). MIDI ticks on the main-loop poll: the ISR
replay and the RTC pump are both released by the SB IRQ, which does not exist here. Every
new branch is behind g_null_open, set only by the model C init: the SB and GUS paths are
unchanged (DOSBox-X: same 52-key audio_vital_status, number-normalised STDOUT identical).
Logs "DOS audio mode: MIDI-only (model C) ...", one "DOS-PORT midionly voice=..." line per
finished clip and a drained_chunks line at shutdown.

DOSBox-X (fixed 40000, 5 Days room 3): sbtype=none + OPL2 / OPL3 and MPU-401-only all play
music (events=1234, midi_tick=poll), clips release after their length (+8..81 ms), exit 0.
Not covered: a stale BLASTER with no card (SDL opens the SB with dsp_ver=255; pre-existing).
